messages.content:
@Mango answering you here in order to leave your article clean:

I haven't watched Puss in Boots (in a while at least, I watched a version when I was a kid), so it's quite an interesting concept you're treating in those regards. On Death of the Endless, I have watched The Sandman TV show and it's pretty much the same concept as the comics one you write about here. I loved that portrayal of Death as gentle to everyone, just fulfilling her duty. And it made me quite emotional given that death can easily be one of my worst fears.

I can't deny that my two RPs will be infused with topics related to that. I always struggle to write simply because of blocks, but I am also afraid of the fact that these RPs' core will be some sort of a battle against that fear in multiple ways. It made me very happy to know that Tolkien's main inspiration for writing was death too. And well, that's a topic you can find since Gilgamesh himself 4000 years ago
